Package: orchestraManifest
Title: The Crop Analytics Orchestra Manifest and Refusal Contract
Version: 0.2.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Max",
           family = "Moldovan",
           email = "max.moldovan@adelaide.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9680-8474"))
Description: A versioned, integrity-hashed and provenance-tracked 'S7'
    contract for the results that crop-analytics components exchange. A
    manifest records what was inferred, which component emitted it, the
    method and seed behind it, the load-bearing payload, and the lineage of
    any upstream manifest it was derived from; a 'SHA-256' hash over
    version-stable serialised bytes lets any consumer verify that the
    payload has not been modified since emission. Consumers declare the
    manifest versions they accept and refuse anything else loudly rather
    than coercing silently across a schema boundary. Companion predicates
    recognise a structured refusal or abstention from any component
    regardless of its object system, so a gate that should stop on a
    declined result cannot sail through it, and grounding tokens propagate
    worst-case so that one unverified input taints a downstream verdict.
    Adapters lift a 'PESTO' ensemble manifest and a 'proxymix' Gaussian
    mixture fit into the contract.
